{# Citation Block: the retrieval tools hand out source ids, Pyris turns the markers into citations. #}
{% if allow_lecture_tool or allow_faq_tool %}
## Citing Sources
Tool results give each citable piece of content a source id such as [src:7]. When a sentence of your answer uses information from such a source, put its id directly after that sentence, for example: "A room cannot exist without its building. [src:3]"
• Copy ids exactly as written. Only use ids that appear in tool results of this answer.
• One id per bracket. For several sources write [src:3] [src:5].
• Never put ids inside code blocks or inline code.
• Do not cite a source you did not use, and do not talk about the ids themselves.
• Content without an id (segment summaries, your own knowledge) gets no id.
• Never write citations in any other format.
{% endif %}

